 See ADR-2607102200 addenda 5 + 7.
 
+## Sprite primitives
+
+A sprite is a vector of primitives in world-unit offsets, all centred on `:dx`/`:dy`
+except `:arc`:
+
+```clojure
+[[:ellipse {:dx :dy :rx :ry :fill}]
+ [:circle  {:dx :dy :r :fill}]
+ [:rect    {:dx :dy :w :h :fill}]
+ [:arc     {:dx :dy :r :a0 :a1 :w :stroke}]   ;; stroked arc — crescents, brims
+ [:image   {:dx :dy :w :h :src :alpha}]       ;; raster art, loaded async
+ [:text    {:dx :dy :text :size :fill}]]      ;; a label the sprite owns
+```
+
+Any part may carry `:anim` — declarative, tick-driven motion (`:rot`/`:pulse`/`:bob`/
+`:sway` around a `:pivot`), so a sprite says how it moves as data.
+
+## Board games
+
+The package was written for a top-down world with an avatar to follow. A board — a shop
+floor, a world map — has no avatar, a known extent, and interaction that is entirely
+"what did the finger land on". Three additions (2026-08-08) cover that:
+
+```clojure
+;; frame a known extent on any screen
+{:render/sprite2d {:camera {:mode :fit :rect [0 0 1600 900] :pad 0.06}}}
+;; or hold a point, with no player entity anywhere
+{:render/sprite2d {:camera {:mode :fixed :x 800 :y 450}}}
+
+;; screen point -> the topmost entity under it (nil for a miss)
+(layout/pick scene snap W H [mx my] 12)   ;; 12px pad for finger-sized targets
+```
+
+`pick` is built on `layout/sprite-bounds`, which unions the sprite's primitive bounds and
+ignores `:anim` — a tap target that twitches with the idle animation is unusable.
+`layout/hit-boxes` returns the whole draw list with screen-space `:box`es if you want to
+draw debug rectangles.
+
+Without `:fixed`/`:fit`, the default camera looks for a `"player"` entity and silently
+anchors at world origin when there isn't one — which looks exactly like a correctly
+centred board right up until the board isn't at the origin.
+
 ## Test
 
 ```sh
 clojure -M:test
 ```
+
+Layout, bounds and picking are pure `.cljc`, so they run on the JVM with no canvas. The
+painter is `.cljs`; calling a painter fn through the facade on the JVM throws with a
+message saying so, which `test/sprite2d_test.clj` pins.
