+   ## :text — a label the sprite owns
+
+   Until now the only text this painter could draw was the screen-space `fx` juice layer:
+   transient, centred on the player, gone in a second. A sprite could not carry a label,
+   which is fine for a creature and wrong for anything a *board* game draws — a machine
+   with a price on it, a tier number, a counter. Those numbers belong to the thing, move
+   with it, and persist. `:text` makes them part of the sprite vector like any other
+   primitive, so they stay readable, diffable, forkable data.
+
+   Canvas text state (`font`/`textAlign`/`textBaseline`) is set and restored around the
+   draw, because it is context-global — leaking it would silently restyle the fx layer.
+
    The *layout* (which sprite, where, in what order) is a pure draw list in
    kami.sprite2d.layout — CLJ-tested on the JVM (camera, W/S orientation, variant swap,
-   depth). This painter only turns that list + the trees into canvas ops."
+   depth, and `pick` for hit-testing). This painter only turns that list + the trees into
+   canvas ops."
   (:require [kami.sprite2d.layout :as layout]))
 
 (defn- css [c] (str "rgba(" (js/Math.round (* 255 (nth c 0))) ","
@@ -99,6 +113,21 @@
                          (catch :default _
                            (swap! images* assoc src {:state :failed :img nil})))
                        (when (not= a 1) (set! (.-globalAlpha ctx) prev)))))))
+    ;; Centred on :dx/:dy like :rect and :image, so a label can be swapped for a shape
+    ;; without moving. Font state is context-global, so it is saved and restored -- the
+    ;; fx juice layer sets its own and must not inherit this one.
+    :text    (let [s (:text o)]
+               (when (and s (not= s ""))
+                 (let [pf (.-font ctx) pa (.-textAlign ctx) pb (.-textBaseline ctx)]
+                   (set! (.-fillStyle ctx) (css (:fill o [1 1 1])))
+                   (set! (.-font ctx) (str (:weight o 800) " " (:size o 24) "px "
+                                           (:family o "Nunito, system-ui, sans-serif")))
+                   (set! (.-textAlign ctx) (:align o "center"))
+                   (set! (.-textBaseline ctx) (:baseline o "middle"))
+                   (.fillText ctx (str s) (:dx o 0) (:dy o 0))
+                   (set! (.-font ctx) pf)
+                   (set! (.-textAlign ctx) pa)
+                   (set! (.-textBaseline ctx) pb))))
     nil))
 
